<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25712" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lămĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμία</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A witch</i> who was said to suck children's blood,
				<i>a sorceress, enchantress</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">neu pransae lamiae vivum puerum extrahat alvo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. A.
					P. 340</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 110, 3</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">5</span></i>, p. 164, 6.—<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lamiae turres,</span>”
				<i>nursery tales</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Val. 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A sort of flatfish</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 24,
				40, § 78</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A species of owl</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Isa.
				34, 14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
